 61FE    61MN B- DECAY (0.709 S)       2013RA17,1985RU05         15NDS    201503
 61FE  H TYP=FUL$AUT=KAZIMIERZ ZUBER, BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=NDS 125, 1 (2015)$       
 61FE2 H CUT=25-Jan-2015$                                                       
 61FE c  2013Ra17: {+61}Mn produced in induced fission of uranium at ISOLDE-CERN
 61FE2c  facility. E(proton)=1.4 GeV beam impinged a UC{-x} target of thickness 
 61FE3c  45 g/cm{+2}. Reaction products where ionized by RILIS and              
 61FE4c  separated based on their A/Q ratio using a High-Resolution Separator.  
 61FE5c  {+61}Mn obtained in the reaction was implanted on an aluminized mylar  
 61FE6c  tape for the decay. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, half-life using      
 61FE7c  three plastic |DE |b detectors and two MiniBall |g-detector clusters.  
 61FE8c  Deduced levels, J, |p, |b feeding intensities, log| {Ift}. Comparison  
 61FE9c  with {+59}Fe data, and with shell-model calculations.                  
 61FE c  1985Ru05: first identification of {+61}Mn from fragmentation of {+82}Se
 61FE2c  beam at 11.5 MeV/nucleon on tungsten target using on-line mass         
 61FE3c  separator. Measured E|g, I|g, |b|g-, |g|g-coin, and T{-1/2} by Ge(Li)  
 61FE4c  and plastic scintillator. Three excited states at 207, 391 and 629 keV 
 61FE5c  were proposed through the observation of five |g rays                  
 61FE c  1999Ha05: 1-GeV proton -induced spallation of uranium UC{-2} target    
 61FE2c  at ISOLDE-CERN facility. The laser ionized Mn isotopes were extracted  
 61FE3c  from the ion source and mass separated. Using tape systems measured    
 61FE4c  |b-delayed neutron multiscaling, E|g and |g|g coincidence. |b-delayed  
 61FE5c  neutron data were collected by multiscaling measurements using         
 61FE6c  Mainz 4|p He neutron counter.                                          
 61FE c  All data are from 2013Ra17                                             
 61FE c  From RADLIST code, deduced total decay energy is 5962 keV {I841}       
 61FE2c  as compared to Q(|b{+-})=7178 keV {I3}, which suggests that the decay  
 61FE3c  scheme is not known well                                               
 61FE cG RI(A)$From |g|g-coin data; transition not seen in singles spectrum     
 61FE cL E$From least-squares fit to E|g values. Reduced                        
 61FE2cL |h{+2}=2.1 is somewhat larger than critical |h{+2}=1.7                 
 61FE cL J$From Adopted Levels. Most of the assignments are based on shell-model
 61FE2cL calculations using GXPF1A interaction corroborated                     
 61FE3cL by |b feedings and associated log| {Ift} values, and also comparison   
 61FE4cL with the decay scheme of {+59}Mn to {+59}Fe                            
